 215:Core/Src/lora.c ****     // LDRO (low data rate optimize): auto-compute from symbol time.
 216:Core/Src/lora.c ****     // Bench-verified 2026-11-08 with corruption map firmware: at SF9/BW62.5
 217:Core/Src/lora.c ****     // (symbol 8.19 ms) every received frame carried 1-5 corrupted bytes with
 218:Core/Src/lora.c ****     // LDRO disabled; identical units at SF7/SF8/SF9-BW125 (symbol <= 4.1 ms)
 219:Core/Src/lora.c ****     // were bit-perfect. The datasheet mandates LDRO only above 16 ms, but
 220:Core/Src/lora.c ****     // this silicon revision needs it from ~8 ms up. SF12 uniformly requires
 221:Core/Src/lora.c ****     // it regardless of silicon revision.
